<title>UK: Portugal sets 13 billion yen dual currency bond.</title>
<headline>Portugal sets 13 billion yen dual currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers IBJ International and New Japan Securities Europe.</p>
<p> BORROWER   PORTUGAL</p>
<p> AMT    13 BLN YEN    COUPON     *5.36     MATURITY    15.MAY.00</p>
<p> TYPE   DUAL-CURRENCY ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    15.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.50	LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    SEMI ANN</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AA3/AA-   DENOMS (K) 500	 SALE LIMS US/UK/PO/JP</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	REDEMPTION IN U.S. DOLLARS.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
